<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Mu'izz ibn Badis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1008">1008</a>–1062</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Mu'izz ibn Badis was Zirid emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> from 1016 to 1062. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a> flourished in his early reign, but around 1048 he broke with the Shia Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a> and recognised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasids</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a> responded by sending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-hilal">Banu Hilal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-sulaym">Banu Sulaym</a> against him; after his defeat at Haydaran in 1052 he left Kairouan for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdia">Mahdia</a> in 1057.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-muizz-ibn-badis.jpg" alt="Al-Mu'izz ibn Badis" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kabyle20 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dinar_of_the_Zirid_emir_al-Mu%27izz_ibn_Badis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
